WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.990
- Hi my name is Kiano I'm
a tasty producer and today

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.340
I'm going to show you
how to be a better baker.

00:00:07.224 --> 00:00:11.410
Pies are such a fun,
simple way to be creative.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.690
You have a crust and you
fill it with generally fruit

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.240
that has a little bit of
sugar, a little bit of spice.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.150
So you kind of have a blank
canvas to decorate it however

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.780
you want, you don't have to
be professional to do it.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.940
Pie decorating can be as
simple or as complicated

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.246
as you want it to be, even if
you don't have proper tools

00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:34.179
you can use the most random
items in your kitchen.

00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:38.700
When you're trying to
customize and like make you pie

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.630
look like your own, you
really can use anything that's

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.513
available to you, use
whatever tools you have

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:47.660
in your kitchen to customize
and make it your own.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.990
I think the fun thing about
baking is that most desserts

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.300
have different components
so when you're cooking

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.040
with other people, everyone can kind

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.690
of take charge of a section of that.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.876
So is you're making a
pie, one person can tackle

00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:03.633
the crust, maybe another
person can tackle the filing.

00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:08.404
For example my sister is
into spices, she will raid

00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:11.850
cabinet, put a little bit of
this, a little bit of that

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.680
in there, so I can pay more
attention to making the crust.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.103
So in the kitchen you're
baking together but everyone

00:01:18.103 --> 00:01:20.970
has a piece so they can put
their own personal flair

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.835
and personality to and they
will all get baked together like

00:01:23.835 --> 00:01:26.794
one cool little product but
everyone had their hands in it.

00:01:26.794 --> 00:01:31.794
I haven't lived in my hometown
in over 10 years so anytime

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.040
I go back home my family
immediately requests a pie from me.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.910
It doesn't matter if it's a
holiday, they're like we want

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.790
apple pie period even though
they're asking for the exact

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.021
same thing time and after
time again it's a fun,

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:48.310
creative challenge of how
do I take the exact same

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:51.180
ingredients but make it
new where everyone is still

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.330
like whoa I've never seen that before.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:56.050
Customizing decoration
is a huge part of it.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.420
There's so many ways of
transforming a familiar dish

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.588
so that excitement never fades.

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:05.064
Very few people in my family
bakes, even to this day when

00:02:05.064 --> 00:02:09.560
I return home for any holiday
I am working with bare

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.061
minimum equipment, when I
am cooking with my family

00:02:13.061 --> 00:02:16.290
I am always trying to
get creative and make

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.650
desserts with what we all ready have.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.760
So I'm like all right how can
I make dessert for this dinner

00:02:22.719 --> 00:02:23.840
without cluttering the
family kitchen with things

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.402
that they aren't gonna use all the time.

00:02:26.402 --> 00:02:29.050
It's so easy to say I
want to get into baking

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.701
and then buy all of the
stuff but really you can make

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.993
dessert with a lot fewer
things than you need.

00:02:34.993 --> 00:02:37.897
You can get creative with
what you all ready have

00:02:37.897 --> 00:02:41.040
around the house, there's so many ways

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.351
you can present your dish
and it doesn't always

00:02:44.351 --> 00:02:47.920
have to be exactly as the recipe told you.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.005
I've always viewed a recipe
as a piece of inspiration

00:02:51.005 --> 00:02:54.825
or kind of an over view
guideline of what to do

00:02:54.825 --> 00:02:58.770
bu then the real joy of
home cooking is that it's

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.020
your kitchen, it's your rules,
you can do what you want.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.670
If it says put one teaspoon
of cinnamon and you don't

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:05.850
like cinnamon put something else in there.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.876
There's a lot of room to
customize and make your desserts

00:03:09.876 --> 00:03:12.920
a lot more creative and
unique, which is what people

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.200
are going to respond too when you put

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.340
it in front of them because
it's gonna be different

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.350
from what you can buy
from your grocery store

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.680
and you have more control
over what you're making

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.340
and you can make it fit
to the equation better.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.310
There's this whole world
of how you visually present

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.403
what you're making that
really can transition you into

00:03:31.403 --> 00:03:35.330
a whole different realm of
challenging what the tried

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.650
and true is and you can
really get creative.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:42.351
So a dessert that I made
that was more of a challenge

00:03:42.351 --> 00:03:44.870
was making a Charlotte Royale.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.100
It is a old school English
cake, when I am making stuff

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.440
at home I want to make
things that I want to eat.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.890
That means seeing this
really classic recipe

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.040
but switching out the parts that I wish

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.480
I could have it as I could never buy.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.342
So with the Charlotte Royale
I made I am a huge fan

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:05.840
of cheesecake, it is one of
my favorite types of dessert

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.980
and I decided to fill the
Charlotte Royale with cheesecake

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.140
instead of Buvarian cream because I think

00:04:12.177 --> 00:04:13.553
what you're making should excite you.

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:16.290
So event though it was by
the book one way when you're

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.840
cooking for yourself and
for your friends you wanna

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.450
make it tailored to your audience,

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.760
you make it how you're gonna enjoy it.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.520
Cake making has a lot more
moving parts that can go

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.350
a little bit more wrong
once you know what makes

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.000
a great cake batter,
what makes a great icing.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.170
You can start playing
around with how you present

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.070
that and you can change the shape

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.930
and decorate it really cool and pretty.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.810
With any thing practice
makes perfect, so when you're

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.901
making that batter you want
to make sure at no point

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.951
are you over working that batter.

00:04:47.951 --> 00:04:51.051
A big mistake you can make
is wanting to have the batter

00:04:51.051 --> 00:04:55.914
look nice and smooth and
like luxurious where to make

00:04:55.914 --> 00:04:59.346
a really good cake batter you
want it to be just combined.

00:04:59.346 --> 00:05:03.760
So that everything is there
otherwise if you're overworking

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.420
it you're actually you're
gonna make a really tough cake.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.235
It's always great to having
that moment where you put that

00:05:09.235 --> 00:05:11.859
thing you spent all
afternoon making on the table

00:05:11.859 --> 00:05:15.530
in front of people and
getting that wow reaction.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.607
You want to see people excited.

00:05:17.607 --> 00:05:20.924
To make a beautiful dessert
it's not about doing

00:05:20.924 --> 00:05:23.980
the most complicated
thing, the recipe itself

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.884
can be very simple, it's
how you customize it

00:05:26.884 --> 00:05:29.700
and stylize it just by putting your own

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.910
personality into it and getting creative.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.002
With cake making you generally
have multiple components

00:05:35.002 --> 00:05:39.059
and to make sure in the end
you end up with a beautiful

00:05:39.059 --> 00:05:43.920
cake you really have to pay
attention to every element

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.850
and take your time, your never being

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:48.100
too over ambitious with any stock.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.250
So if there is a part that
you're maybe not as comfortable

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.511
with take a shortcut make it simpler,

00:05:53.511 --> 00:05:56.090
you don't need every element of what

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.960
you are doing to be brand new to you.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.955
So to make something
different that people may have

00:06:00.955 --> 00:06:05.955
not seen before I decided to
do this rippled ombre effect.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.862
Borrowing inspiration from
another type of cake called

00:06:10.862 --> 00:06:14.430
a zebra cake, each color pushes
out the previous creating

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.722
this nice ripple effect but
instead of having two colors

00:06:18.722 --> 00:06:21.450
back and forth in tiny quantities.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.403
I decided to do four
shades of brown to white

00:06:24.403 --> 00:06:27.620
so it took something not
people are familiar with

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.350
the chocolate cheesecake,
it's no bake and whip

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.190
it up in 10 minutes and
through customizing it.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:36.453
It turned into a very
beautiful and unique dessert.

00:06:38.137 --> 00:06:41.270
There's so many things that
could go wrong while baking.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.110
You can crack a
cheesecake, or maybe forgot

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.840
to spray your cake and it
will not come out the pan.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.890
Or you over baked your cookies
and they're hard as a brick.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.761
Don't worry about it you can
salvage it and get a little

00:06:52.761 --> 00:06:55.610
creative to make something
new and could still have

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.650
a really great dessert in the end.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.158
I think it's really important
to know that just because

00:07:00.158 --> 00:07:03.380
something didn't turn out as you intended,

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.960
does not mean it's always a lost cause.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.590
You can always repurpose
what you've all ready made

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.560
and make another cool dessert out of it

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:16.054
or sometimes you can even fix
it and cover up your mistake.

00:07:16.054 --> 00:07:19.260
When looking at a recipe to
make the first thing to do

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.008
is figure out what part is
science and what part is flavor.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:25.302
Science I'm not messing with,
I'm not messing with how

00:07:25.302 --> 00:07:29.850
it's going to rise or structurally
work but with the flavor

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:33.220
that's when it becomes customizable.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.130
When you're making things
in your own kitchen your

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:39.444
imagination has no limit you
can put whatever ingredients

00:07:39.444 --> 00:07:43.860
you want you can make it
shaped however you want.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.640
It really is a question
of your personality

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.740
or what you did that day,
you could've have been

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.510
to the farmers market and saw beautiful

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.580
strawberries you're gonna use that.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:55.940
It's putting a lot more
of yourself into the food

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.190
than you actually expected to.

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:01.910
Baking is inherently a celebratory food,

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.922
every occasion we have in life
usually has an accompanied

00:08:04.922 --> 00:08:09.922
dessert, it's generally for
something or for someone.

00:08:10.232 --> 00:08:14.310
And I think there is nothing
more awkward or fearful

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:17.000
than putting something in front of someone

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.050
that you're like hey I'm
expecting you to eat this

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:23.350
and in their mind they're like
ew I don't want to eat that.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.620
How can I pretend that I like it.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.330
It's always a goal to but
something in front of people

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.800
that they're genuinely excited to try.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.120
When you're baking for other people, when

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:36.840
you present it to them
there's so much appreciation

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.722
that comes into that, even
though it might not be perfect

00:08:39.722 --> 00:08:43.640
every time especially when
you're starting to bake out.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:46.560
But when you take time
and effort to make things

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.730
for the people you care about
it does not go unnoticed.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:53.300
And you have a secondary reward
that you get to make things

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.930
for people but then after
that you get to share it with

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.438
them as well and you get to
sit down with your friends,

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.600
stand with your family over the food

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.930
that you've just made for them.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.503
Enjoy each other's
company have the laughs,

00:09:05.432 --> 00:09:07.183
blow out the candles and
just have a good time.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.440
Even when you're baking
yes stuff can go wrong

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.700
it might not be exactly as you envisioned

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.270
it and it can't be perfect all the time.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.700
But when you're baking for
other people they're gonna

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.400
appreciate that you took the time,

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.760
put the energy into making
something really special

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:25.560
for them and that's
always nice to share food

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.520
with other people that you care about.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.353
- [Male] Oh yes!

00:09:29.948 --> 00:09:33.031
(upbeat theme music)

